From 7021b5bb1dd5815e3055ec4b674075d5de7dcce9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: IMD Ember <operator@imdember.invalid>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 03:34:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] Swarm audit f6bd50ad: lower-nonce payment must succeed,
 drop a failed note by hash, refuse bundler overrides; GOLD review record

- Finding 1: the lower-nonce exception accepts only a successful payment (a revert uses no order id).
- Finding 2: a failed payment's crediting note is dropped by its own hash, never by order, so a
  second tab's new payment of the order keeps its note.
- Finding 3: ESBUILD_BINARY_PATH and NAPI_RS_NATIVE_LIBRARY_PATH are refused like WRANGLER_BUILD_*.
- The GOLD panel shows a collapsed record of this review (job, report, reviewed source, the three
  findings and their status as the site maintainer reports it), in every panel state.

5 mutations, each caught.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
